To prevent a `Dialog` or `Drawer` from closing, e.g. due to validation, the `onClose` function can now return **false**.

**EXAMPLE USAGE:**
```jsx
<Drawer
  onClose={() => {
    const valid = runValidation();
    if (!valid) {
      return false;
    }

    closeDrawer();
  }}
/>
```

Azure OpenAI uses a long-running operation for its DALL-E image generation capability. The polling response format is a strict subset of the final, data-bearing response format. This change takes advantage of that subset nature by constraining the definition of AOAI's image generation custom LRO to use the same code generation model for both status and final response payloads -- which, in turn, allows us to sidestep some avoidable challenges with current discrepancies in code generation behavior across languages.

An example status response body:
```json
"ResponseBody": {
  "created": 1687457362,
  id": "...",
  status": "running"
}
```

And an example final response body:
```json
"ResponseBody": {
  "created": 1687457362,
  "expires": 1687543766,
  "id": "...",
  "result": {
    "created": 1687457362,
    "data": [
      {
        "url": "https://dalleproduse.blob.core.windows.net/private/images/foo.png"
      },
    ]
  },
  "status": "succeeded"
}
```

The status format seamlessly deserializes (partially) into the larger response model and allows everything to work smoothly without a separate model for the subset status payload.

