There's a couple fixes and enhancements here:

1) Let client specify the real UUID of the row on Insert. ovsdb-server has supported this for a couple years already.

2) Named UUIDs being removed from the _uuid field when calling NewRow() causes some pain for some testcases I'm working on; remove that hack and harmonize the named UUID handling between Insert and Update by just removing the _uuid column entirely, which ovsdb-server ignores anyway.

3) Process the UUIDName in each Operation first to build the mapping table, then make a second pass to expand the named UUIDs in each Operation's arguments. This allows using a named UUID in an earlier operation that is realized in a later one.  For example, adding an OVS Port to a Bridge with ovs-vsctl will update the Bridge's Ports field first and then create the Port after, which fails with the existing single-pass Named UUID expansion.

```
    {
        "op":"update"
        "table":"Bridge",
        "row":{
            "ports":[
                "set",[["named-uuid","row485700fe_28a9_46f3_8281_793f6d0fabf5"],["uuid","502ae6bd-96f3-487e-9bbe-b76a3b25fff3"]]
            ]
        },
        "where":[["_uuid","==",["uuid","056a9de5-1861-467f-a109-a2ffcd362350"]]],
    },
    {
        "op":"insert",
        "table":"Port",
        "row":{
            "name":"dummy1",
            "interfaces":["named-uuid","rowa3be83f3_2582_40b8_8b49_68e8b81cee6e"]
        },
        "uuid-name":"row485700fe_28a9_46f3_8281_793f6d0fabf5"
    },
```

When having multiple types of markers on the map that have hierarchy rules to them which requires setting different `z-index` being able to pass a different `className` to the Marker component is necessary.

```css
.secondary {
  z-index: 1;
}

.primary {
  z-index: 2;
}
```

```jsx
<Map>
  <Marker className="secondary">Secondary</Marker>
  <Marker className="primary">Primary</Marker>
</Map>
```

